1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:05,647
Before your team can answer customers' texts, the site needs to be connected

2
00:00:05,647 --> 00:00:09,670
to an SMS provider, and told where each number's texts should go.

3
00:00:09,670 --> 00:00:13,977
This video walks through that setup, from the features to a test text:

4
00:00:13,977 --> 00:00:19,700
the provider, the numbers, the entry point, the permissions, and the address used for pictures.

5
00:00:24,300 --> 00:00:26,665
First, turn on the features.

6
00:00:26,665 --> 00:00:32,440
One feature, SMS Messaging Channel, brings the inbox and everything it needs.

7
00:00:33,190 --> 00:00:38,854
Second, connect an SMS provider such as Twilio, and choose the default one.

8
00:00:38,854 --> 00:00:42,770
Third, add each of your numbers as a text address.

9
00:00:43,520 --> 00:00:48,371
Fourth, add an entry point, which says where the texts of a number

10
00:00:48,371 --> 00:00:50,796
go, to an agent or to a queue.

11
00:00:50,796 --> 00:00:54,300
Fifth, give the right roles their permissions.

12
00:00:55,050 --> 00:01:00,122
Last, give your provider the webhook address of the site, so that customers'

13
00:01:00,122 --> 00:01:02,658
texts and delivery receipts arrive.

14
00:01:02,658 --> 00:01:04,390
Then send a test text.

15
00:01:08,690 --> 00:01:12,059
Open Tools, Features, and search for messaging.

16
00:01:12,059 --> 00:01:14,283
Enable SMS Messaging Channel.

17
00:01:14,283 --> 00:01:19,876
It enables the Messaging Workspace, the channel addresses, the work queues and the

18
00:01:19,876 --> 00:01:22,800
provider webhook inbox together with it.

19
00:01:23,265 --> 00:01:26,678
Omnichannel Messaging Routed Distribution is optional.

20
00:01:26,678 --> 00:01:30,718
Enable it only when you want a queue to hand out conversations to

21
00:01:30,718 --> 00:01:32,823
the least busy available agent.

22
00:01:32,823 --> 00:01:37,033
Enabling the workspace on its own gives you an inbox with nothing to

23
00:01:37,033 --> 00:01:38,455
send or receive on.

24
00:01:42,655 --> 00:01:45,317
Open Settings, Communication, SMS.

25
00:01:45,317 --> 00:01:51,039
On the Providers tab, Default SMS provider chooses the provider that sends texts

26
00:01:51,039 --> 00:01:54,365
for every number that does not name its own.

27
00:01:54,819 --> 00:01:57,528
Each provider you enable adds a tab.

28
00:01:57,528 --> 00:02:02,751
On the Twilio tab, tick Enable Twilio Provider, and enter the Phone Number,

29
00:02:02,751 --> 00:02:06,813
the Account SID and the Auth Token that Twilio gives you.

30
00:02:06,813 --> 00:02:09,199
The token is never shown again.

31
00:02:09,653 --> 00:02:13,247
The Webhook URL field shows the address to give Twilio.

32
00:02:13,247 --> 00:02:17,901
In the Twilio console, set the number's incoming message to this address.

33
00:02:17,901 --> 00:02:21,789
Customers' texts and delivery receipts then reach the inbox.

34
00:02:21,789 --> 00:02:25,323
The site must be reachable from the internet for this.

35
00:02:29,518 --> 00:02:31,855
Open Tools, Testing, SMS Test.

36
00:02:31,855 --> 00:02:37,244
Pick a provider, type a phone number in international format, and click Send.

37
00:02:37,244 --> 00:02:41,075
A notice says whether the provider accepted the text.

38
00:02:41,075 --> 00:02:43,218
Use a number you can check.

39
00:02:47,435 --> 00:02:53,089
Open Interaction Center, Management, Omnichannel Addresses, and edit a number.

40
00:02:53,089 --> 00:02:57,196
The Phone number is the number in international format.

41
00:02:57,196 --> 00:03:01,235
Under Used for, Text messages makes it a text address.

42
00:03:01,694 --> 00:03:04,910
Provider chooses which provider owns this number.

43
00:03:04,910 --> 00:03:09,297
Leave it on Use the tenant-default provider, or pin the number to one

44
00:03:09,297 --> 00:03:11,754
provider when you use more than one.

45
00:03:12,213 --> 00:03:16,854
Agents who text from this number lists the people who may send texts from it.

46
00:03:16,854 --> 00:03:21,383
Leave it empty when the number is a department number that a queue answers.

47
00:03:25,577 --> 00:03:32,279
Open Interaction Center, Management, Inbound entry points, and edit the entry point of the number.

48
00:03:32,279 --> 00:03:37,177
Numbers lists the numbers it answers, and Route to chooses an agent, a

49
00:03:37,177 --> 00:03:38,917
queue or an AI agent.

50
00:03:39,372 --> 00:03:44,607
For a queue, Target queue chooses the queue, and Queue distribution chooses the

51
00:03:44,607 --> 00:03:49,042
shared pool or routed distribution, as the routing video explains.

52
00:03:49,497 --> 00:03:54,113
Auto-reply sends a short answer to a customer who writes, at most once

53
00:03:54,113 --> 00:03:55,875
a day per conversation.

54
00:03:55,875 --> 00:04:01,037
Closed auto-reply answers when the Business hours calendar says you are closed.

55
00:04:05,238 --> 00:04:09,285
Open Access Control, Roles and edit the role of your agents.

56
00:04:09,285 --> 00:04:14,313
Use the messaging workspace opens the inbox, and one of the view permissions

57
00:04:14,313 --> 00:04:17,256
decides which conversations a person sees:

58
00:04:17,256 --> 00:04:21,058
their own, their queues' unclaimed ones, or all of them.

59
00:04:21,526 --> 00:04:26,840
Send group messages lets a person send broadcasts, and Manage the messaging workspace

60
00:04:26,840 --> 00:04:29,001
lets a person manage templates.

61
00:04:29,001 --> 00:04:34,316
The permissions cover every channel, and there is no permission for a single channel.

62
00:04:38,506 --> 00:04:41,997
Customers can send pictures, and agents can send them too.

63
00:04:41,997 --> 00:04:46,197
The provider downloads each picture from your site, so the site must be

64
00:04:46,197 --> 00:04:48,052
reachable from the internet.

65
00:04:48,052 --> 00:04:51,979
The link is built from the Base URL in Settings, General, and from

66
00:04:51,979 --> 00:04:54,706
the address of the request when it is empty.

67
00:04:56,306 --> 00:04:58,527
Twilio is not the only choice.

68
00:04:58,527 --> 00:05:03,831
Telnyx and Azure Communication Services add their own tab and their own webhook,

69
00:05:03,831 --> 00:05:07,346
and a number can be pinned to any enabled provider.

70
00:05:08,096 --> 00:05:13,622
Azure Event Grid, which receives Azure Communication Services events, and Azure Blob Storage,

71
00:05:13,622 --> 00:05:17,194
which keeps message pictures, have no screen in the admin.

72
00:05:17,194 --> 00:05:21,156
They are set up in the site's configuration, with your developer.

73
00:05:25,356 --> 00:05:29,944
A shop connects one number, points it at a Support queue, and answers

74
00:05:29,944 --> 00:05:32,696
texts from a shared inbox the same day.

75
00:05:33,446 --> 00:05:37,793
A company with two brands pins each number to its own provider, and

76
00:05:37,793 --> 00:05:39,876
routes each to its own queue.

77
00:05:40,626 --> 00:05:44,359
A team tests a new number with the SMS Test page before it

78
00:05:44,359 --> 00:05:46,166
tells customers about it.

79
00:05:48,166 --> 00:05:52,277
Features, provider, numbers, entry point and permissions:

80
00:05:52,277 --> 00:05:55,930
five steps from a new site to an inbox that works.

81
00:05:55,930 --> 00:05:57,626
Thanks for watching.

